  "details": "I make use of a personalized semver scheme when I upload my Avatars. As of lately, I've noticed that the order of Numbers are completely out of order when sorting Avatars by Name.\n\nWhen I say this, I mean that VRChat cannot tell the difference between 1's, 10's, or 100's whatsoever when looking at an Avatar List.\n\nCurrent Broken Behavior:\n\nv2.1.43 is < than v2.1.5, which is obviously incorrect\n\nv1.0.55 is < than v1.0.3, which is obviously incorrect\n\nv2.16.10 is < than v2.16.2, which is obviously incorrect\n\nExpected Behavior:\n\nv2.1.43 should be > than v2.1.5\n\nv1.0.30 should be > than v1.0.4\n\nv2.16.10 should be > than v2.16.2\n\nEven without extra decimals when comparing different versions, a 10 is considered less than 5. This includes the 100's, where a 100 is considered less than 50.\n\nThat specifically is very annoying and should be a very simple problem to fix. Like, seriously. A 10 is greater than 5, and a 100 is greater than 50. That’s a natural sorting order.",
